          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "maratona comes from Greek, from the name of a town, which is built on márathon \"fennel\" (EtymDB): the story goes that a runner carried news of a victory from there."
            }
          ]
        },
